   "Stripping densely adherent matrix from an exposed nerve risks permanent paralysis that outweighs the benefit of complete removal now.",
   "Monitoring is most valuable precisely when the nerve is exposed and being manipulated; stopping it removes a safety check.",
   "Radiation has no role in benign cholesteatoma and would not reliably control residual keratinizing epithelium."
